-- title:
--   Pull-back of an iterated twist by invertible ideal sheaves
-- statement:
--   Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes, $m \in \mathbb{N}$, let $K : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to Y.\mathrm{IdealSheafData}$ be a family of quasi-coherent ideal sheaves on $Y$ with exponents $\mathrm{pos}, \mathrm{neg} : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb{N}$, and let $C : \iota \to Y.\mathrm{IdealSheafData}$ be a family indexed by a finite type $\iota$, with exponents $\mathrm{aplus}, \mathrm{aminus} : \iota \to \mathbb{N}$. Assume every $K j$ and every $C F$ satisfies `IsInvertible`, i.e. each point of $Y$ lies in a basic open $D(s)$ of an affine open on which the ideal is generated by a single non-zero-divisor, and assume the same of the inverse-image ideals $(K j).\mathrm{comap}\,f$ and $(C F).\mathrm{comap}\,f$ on $X$. Then there exists an isomorphism in the category $X.\mathrm{Modules}$ between the pull-back along $f$ of the right-nested tensor product, folded over `List.finRange m`, of the duals $((K j)^{\mathrm{pos}\,j}).\mathrm{invModule}$ and the ideal modules $((K j)^{\mathrm{neg}\,j}).\mathrm{module}$, with innermost factor $(\prod_F (C F)^{\mathrm{aplus}\,F}).\mathrm{invModule} \otimes (\prod_F (C F)^{\mathrm{aminus}\,F}).\mathrm{module}$, and the expression of exactly the same shape built from the ideals $(K j).\mathrm{comap}\,f$ and $(C F).\mathrm{comap}\,f$ on $X$. Here $I.\mathrm{module}$ is the kernel of the unit map to the pushforward of the unit along the closed immersion of the subscheme cut out by $I$, and $I.\mathrm{invModule}$ is its dual, the internal hom into the monoidal unit. The assertion is the non-emptiness of the type of such isomorphisms, not a designated one.
--
--   This is the compatibility of divisorial (twisting) sheaves with pull-back: for effective Cartier divisors whose inverse images remain Cartier, $f^{*}\mathcal{O}(\pm Z) \cong \mathcal{O}(\pm f^{-1}Z)$, propagated through an iterated tensor product of such twists by the monoidal structure of pull-back, together with the multiplicativity of $\mathrm{comap}$ on powers and finite products. It is used in the study of relative effective Cartier divisors and relative Picard functors, for instance when comparing the Poincaré bundle with twists pulled back along a change of curve or along a point section.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_Modules_nonempty_pullback_foldr_twist_iso.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicGeometry_IdealSheafModule
import Definitions.Def_SheafOfModules_Monoidal
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_RelCartier

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory AlgebraicGeometry

theorem AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.nonempty_pullback_foldr_twist_iso
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) {m : ℕ} (K : Fin m → Y.IdealSheafData) (pos neg : Fin m → ℕ)
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (C : ι → Y.IdealSheafData) (aplus aminus : ι → ℕ)
    (hK : ∀ j, (K j).IsInvertible) (hC : ∀ F, (C F).IsInvertible)
    (hK' : ∀ j, ((K j).comap f).IsInvertible) (hC' : ∀ F, ((C F).comap f).IsInvertible) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj
        ((List.finRange m).foldr (fun j N => (K j ^ pos j).invModule ⊗ (K j ^ neg j).module ⊗ N)
          ((∏ F, C F ^ aplus F).invModule ⊗ (∏ F, C F ^ aminus F).module)) ≅
      (List.finRange m).foldr (fun j N => ((K j).comap f ^ pos j).invModule ⊗ ((K j).comap f ^ neg j).module ⊗ N)
        ((∏ F, (C F).comap f ^ aplus F).invModule ⊗ (∏ F, (C F).comap f ^ aminus F).module)) := by sorry
